{
  "task": "# Stage 04 — Spawning and dodge score\n\nBuild this stage in the existing Godot 4.7.2 project. Use GDScript and Godot Editor MCP. Assets are under `res://assets/`. Do not add dependencies.\n\nFirst check `godot_health_check` and project info. If disconnected, retry the health check up to eight times. Confirm the bridge project path matches the current directory containing `project.godot`; stop and report if it remains disconnected or points elsewhere. Inspect saved work before editing. Reuse anything already correct; make only needed changes. Fix tool errors using the returned details. After two failed corrections to the same error, stop and report it. Save changes and verify them. Work without asking for a plan or approval.\n\nImplement the game only. Do not write or edit `test/`, test helpers, Vitest configuration, or test results, and do not run `npm test`. The benchmark host owns final testing; your final response is the handoff. Check changed work with Godot inspection, parse checks, or a short runtime check; report what each check actually showed.\n\n- Inspect `res://main.tscn` and `res://scripts/meteor.gd`. Under Main, add or repair `Meteors` (`Node2D`); meteors can use z=0 between Background (-10) and Player (10).\n- Attach `res://scripts/main.gd` to Main. Declare `@export var meteor_scene: PackedScene = preload(\"res://scenes/meteor.tscn\")` with the quoted path. Spawn under Meteors at random x=45..915, y=-60, using all three variants and varied fall speeds. Start near 1.2 seconds between spawns and gradually approach a safe floor near 0.45 seconds.\n- Keep explicit `score` and `elapsed_time` state. Connect each meteor's `passed` signal; award exactly one point only when it exits below the playfield. No points on spawn or collision. Add no damage or HUD yet.\n- Save, parse-check `main.gd`, and run a short headless smoke check. Report runtime errors. After two failed fixes for the same parse error, stop and report it.\n\n## Final report\n\nState what you completed, the Godot checks you ran and their results, and any failures or unverified requirements. Say “Ready for host verification” when finished. Do not claim that host tests passed.\n",
